# Task 1 implementation report

## Files changed

- `core/pit_diagnosis/__init__.py`: public exports for the PIT diagnosis rulebook API.
- `core/pit_diagnosis/models.py`: frozen enums and dataclasses, recursively immutable mappings/policies, and field validation.
- `core/pit_diagnosis/rulebook.py`: duplicate-key-safe canonical JSON loading, canonical SHA-256, rulebook construction, one-of N.NEWNESS resolution, and fail-closed fidelity assessment.
- `config/pit_canslim_rulebook_v1.json`: version `pit-canslim-v1`, five approved source citations, and all 23 approved rule records with fixed policies.
- `tests/test_pit_diagnosis_rulebook.py`: rulebook schema, one-of N, missing/unknown evidence, canonical JSON, and proxy validation tests.

## Design decisions

The public model types are frozen dataclasses. Rulebook and policy mappings are `MappingProxyType`; nested policy objects/lists are recursively converted to immutable mappings/tuples. Enum constructors reject values outside the closed contract. Canonical JSON rejects duplicate keys and non-finite constants, and hashes sorted compact UTF-8 JSON with `allow_nan=False`. Fidelity evaluation rejects unknown or missing outcome IDs, resolves `N.NEWNESS` only from a passed catalyst or passed new-high branch, validates approved proxy IDs against declared proxy rules, and never marks failed, unavailable, unimplemented, or unapproved required rules promotion-eligible.

